@startuml malformed-event-routing
title US-09: Malformed Event Routing - Bad Event Sent to DLQ

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

queue "Kafka\nadsb.raw / ais.raw" as Kafka
participant "Position\nConsumer" as Consumer
queue "Kafka\nadsb.dlq / ais.dlq" as DLQ

Kafka -> Consumer : consume raw event

Consumer -> Consumer : attempt to parse event

alt event is valid
  Consumer -> Consumer : normalise and forward\nto position.normalized
  note over Consumer
    Happy path - processing continues.
  end note

else event is malformed or unparseable
  note over Consumer
    Bad payload - missing required fields,
    invalid coordinates, unrecognised format.
    Do not crash. Do not drop silently.
  end note

  Consumer -> DLQ : publish to adsb.dlq / ais.dlq\n{ raw_payload, rejection_reason, timestamp_ms,\n  consumer_id, source_topic, source_offset }

  note over DLQ
    Original raw payload preserved.
    Rejection reason attached.
    Event is inspectable and recoverable.
    No data is silently lost.
  end note

  Consumer -> Kafka : commit offset and continue\nprocessing next event
end

@enduml
